#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:162
msgid "Virtual Switch Prerequisites"
msgstr "Requisitos previos del Switch Virtual"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:164
msgid "Before creating a Virtual Switch, ensure the following:"
msgstr "Antes de crear un Switch Virtual, asegúrese de lo siguiente:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:166
msgid ""
"**Physical NICs are cabled and up** on each host that will participate in"
" the Virtual Switch."
msgstr ""
"**Las NICs físicas están cableadas y activas** en cada host que participará en"
" el Switch Virtual."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:167
msgid ""
"**Upstream switch ports are configured** for the desired mode "
"(access/trunk, VLAN IDs, and LACP when using 802.3ad)."
msgstr ""
"**Los puertos del switch upstream están configurados** para el modo deseado "
"(acceso/trunk, IDs de VLAN y LACP cuando se usa 802.3ad)."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:168
msgid ""
"**Consistent NIC naming** across hosts if using uniform uplinks, or "
"identify per-host NIC names in advance."
msgstr ""
"**Nombres de NIC consistentes** entre hosts si se utilizan uplinks uniformes, o "
"identifique los nombres de NIC por host con anticipación."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:169
msgid ""
"**MTU support end-to-end** — All devices in the network path (switches, "
"routers, storage arrays) must support the configured MTU (especially 9000"
" for jumbo frames)."
msgstr ""
"**Soporte de MTU de extremo a extremo** — Todos los dispositivos en la ruta de red (switches, "
"routers, matrices de almacenamiento) deben soportar el MTU configurado (especialmente 9000"
" para tramas jumbo)."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:170
msgid ""
"**iSCSI multipath** should be configured at the OS/protocol layer if "
"using iSCSI storage."
msgstr ""
"**iSCSI multipath** debe configurarse en la capa de OS/protocolo si "
"se utiliza almacenamiento iSCSI."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:172
msgid ""
"If a newly installed physical NIC is not available for selection, first "
"add and safely validate it in Netplan, use ``sudo hvmcli interfaces list "
"--filter ethernet`` to confirm host discovery, and refresh the cluster in"
" the UI. See :ref:`hvm-host-prep` for the guarded procedure. Do not use a"
" mutating ``hvmcli virtswitch`` command merely to make an OS interface "
"appear in inventory."
msgstr ""
"Si una NIC física recién instalada no está disponible para selección, primero "
"agréguela y valídela de forma segura en Netplan, use ``sudo hvmcli interfaces list "
"--filter ethernet`` para confirmar el descubrimiento del host, y actualice el clúster en"
" la interfaz de usuario. Consulte :ref:`hvm-host-prep` para el procedimiento guiado. No use un"
" comando ``hvmcli virtswitch`` que modifique el estado simplemente para hacer que una interfaz del SO "
"aparezca en el inventario."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:175
msgid "Adding a Virtual Switch"
msgstr "Agregar un Switch Virtual"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:177
msgid ""
"Click **Add Virtual Switch** to launch the creation wizard. The wizard "
"guides you through the following steps:"
msgstr ""
"Haga clic en **Add Virtual Switch** para iniciar el asistente de creación. El asistente "
"le guía a través de los siguientes pasos:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:180
msgid "Step 1: Select Type"
msgstr "Paso 1: Seleccionar tipo"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:182
msgid "Enter a **Name** for the Virtual Switch (maximum 12 characters)"
msgstr "Ingrese un **Name** para el Switch Virtual (máximo 12 caracteres)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:183
msgid "Select one or more **traffic types** for this Virtual Switch"
msgstr "Seleccione uno o más **tipos de tráfico** para este Switch Virtual"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:184
msgid "Click **Next**"
msgstr "Haga clic en **Next**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:186
#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:265
#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:284
msgid "Note"
msgstr "Nota"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:186
msgid ""
"The Virtual Switch name is limited to 12 characters because it is used to"
" derive the underlying Linux bridge name (name + ``-br`` suffix), which "
"must fit within the Linux 15-character interface name limit."
msgstr ""
"El nombre del Switch Virtual está limitado a 12 caracteres porque se utiliza para"
" derivar el nombre del bridge Linux subyacente (nombre + sufijo ``-br``), que "
"debe caber dentro del límite de 15 caracteres para nombres de interfaz de Linux."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:188
#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:236
msgid "Tip"
msgstr "Consejo"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:188
msgid ""
"The default ``vs0`` created during cluster provisioning can be renamed "
"and edited, but it should not be deleted unless an alternative VM Network"
" Virtual Switch is in place. At least one Virtual Switch with the VM "
"Network traffic type must exist for VMs to have network connectivity."
msgstr ""
"El ``vs0`` predeterminado creado durante el aprovisionamiento del clúster puede renombrarse "
"y editarse, pero no debe eliminarse a menos que exista un Switch Virtual de Red de VM"
" alternativo. Debe existir al menos un Switch Virtual con el tipo de tráfico "
"Red de VM para que las VMs tengan conectividad de red."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:191
msgid "Step 2: Configure"
msgstr "Paso 2: Configurar"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:193
msgid "Configure the physical uplinks and bond mode for the Virtual Switch."
msgstr "Configure los uplinks físicos y el modo de bond para el Switch Virtual."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:195
msgid "Configure step - Uniform uplinks with No Bonding"
msgstr "Paso de configuración - Uplinks uniformes sin bonding"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:195
#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:228
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_configure_uniform.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_configure_uniform.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:198
msgid "**Bond Mode**"
msgstr "**Modo de bond**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:200
msgid "Select how multiple NICs are aggregated:"
msgstr "Seleccione cómo se agregan múltiples NICs:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:206
msgid "Bond Mode"
msgstr "Modo de bond"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:208
msgid "**No Bonding**"
msgstr "**Sin bonding**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:209
msgid ""
"Single NIC per host. No redundancy at the link level. Maximum 1 NIC per "
"host."
msgstr ""
"NIC única por host. Sin redundancia a nivel de enlace. Máximo 1 NIC por "
"host."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:210
msgid "**Active Backup**"
msgstr "**Active Backup**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:211
msgid ""
"One NIC active, one standby. Automatic failover if the active link fails."
" No switch-side configuration required."
msgstr ""
"Una NIC activa, una en espera. Conmutación por error automática si el enlace activo falla."
" No se requiere configuración en el switch."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:212
msgid "**LACP (802.3ad)**"
msgstr "**LACP (802.3ad)**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:213
msgid ""
"Both NICs participate in an 802.3ad bond. The connected upstream switch "
"ports must belong to the same compatible LACP group."
msgstr ""
"Ambas NICs participan en un bond 802.3ad. Los puertos del switch upstream conectados "
"deben pertenecer al mismo grupo LACP compatible."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:215
msgid "Bond mode dropdown showing available options"
msgstr "Menú desplegable de modo de bond mostrando las opciones disponibles"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:215
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_configure_bond_modes.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_configure_bond_modes.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:218
#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:335
msgid "Warning"
msgstr "Advertencia"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:218
msgid ""
"When using **LACP (802.3ad)**, configure the upstream physical switch "
"ports for the same LACP group before applying the Virtual Switch. "
"Mismatched configurations can cause connectivity loss."
msgstr ""
"Al usar **LACP (802.3ad)**, configure los puertos del switch físico upstream "
"para el mismo grupo LACP antes de aplicar el Switch Virtual. "
"Las configuraciones no coincidentes pueden causar pérdida de conectividad."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:220
msgid ""
"Do not assume that an Active Backup bond receives universal MII polling, "
"up-delay, or down-delay values automatically. These settings can vary by "
"HVM release and networking backend, and automatic defaults are not "
"guaranteed. Before carrying production traffic, inspect the effective "
"bond configuration on each host and configure the required values "
"explicitly through tooling supported by that HVM release. Use the product"
" UI or ``hvmcli`` capabilities documented for the installed release; do "
"not copy unverified values from another release or backend."
msgstr ""
"No asuma que un bond Active Backup recibe valores universales de sondeo MII, "
"up-delay o down-delay automáticamente. Estos ajustes pueden variar según "
"la versión de HVM y el backend de red, y los valores predeterminados automáticos no están "
"garantizados. Antes de transportar tráfico de producción, inspeccione la configuración "
"efectiva del bond en cada host y configure los valores requeridos "
"explícitamente a través de las herramientas soportadas por esa versión de HVM. Use la interfaz "
"de usuario del producto o las capacidades de ``hvmcli`` documentadas para la versión instalada; no "
"copie valores no verificados de otra versión o backend."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:222
msgid "**Uplink NICs**"
msgstr "**NICs de uplink**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:224
msgid "Choose how physical NICs are assigned to hosts:"
msgstr "Elija cómo se asignan las NICs físicas a los hosts:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:226
msgid ""
"**Uniform uplinks (all hosts)** — The same NIC(s) are used across all "
"hosts. Select from the available interfaces shown as green-tagged "
"buttons."
msgstr ""
"**Uplinks uniformes (todos los hosts)** — Se utilizan las mismas NICs en todos "
"los hosts. Seleccione de las interfaces disponibles mostradas como botones "
"con etiqueta verde."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:228
msgid "Uniform uplink selection"
msgstr "Selección de uplink uniforme"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:231
msgid ""
"**Set uplink NICs per host** — Different NICs can be selected for each "
"individual host. This is useful when hosts have heterogeneous NIC naming "
"or hardware configurations."
msgstr ""
"**Establecer NICs de uplink por host** — Se pueden seleccionar diferentes NICs para cada "
"host individual. Esto es útil cuando los hosts tienen nombres de NIC heterogéneos "
"o configuraciones de hardware diferentes."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:233
msgid "Per-host uplink selection"
msgstr "Selección de uplink por host"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:233
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_configure_per_host.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_configure_per_host.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:236
msgid ""
"Use **Set uplink NICs per host** when servers in the cluster have "
"different NIC names (e.g., different hardware generations with different "
"PCIe slot assignments)."
msgstr ""
"Use **Set uplink NICs per host** cuando los servidores del clúster tienen "
"diferentes nombres de NIC (por ejemplo, diferentes generaciones de hardware con diferentes "
"asignaciones de ranuras PCIe)."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:238
msgid "**iSCSI Configuration**"
msgstr "**Configuración de iSCSI**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:240
msgid ""
"When **Data (iSCSI)** is the selected traffic type, the configure step "
"enforces specific constraints:"
msgstr ""
"Cuando **Data (iSCSI)** es el tipo de tráfico seleccionado, el paso de configuración "
"aplica restricciones específicas:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:242
msgid "Bond mode is locked to **No Bonding**"
msgstr "El modo de bond está bloqueado en **No Bonding**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:243
msgid "Maximum **1 NIC** per host"
msgstr "Máximo **1 NIC** por host"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:245
msgid ""
"This is because iSCSI relies on multipath I/O at the protocol layer for "
"redundancy, not link-layer bonding."
msgstr ""
"Esto se debe a que iSCSI depende de multipath I/O en la capa de protocolo para "
"la redundancia, no del bonding a nivel de enlace."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:247
msgid "iSCSI configuration showing single interface constraint"
msgstr "Configuración de iSCSI mostrando la restricción de interfaz única"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:247
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_configure_iscsi.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_configure_iscsi.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:251
msgid "Step 3: IPv4 Settings"
msgstr "Paso 3: Configuración IPv4"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:253
msgid ""
"Configure IP addressing for traffic types that require host-level IPs "
"(Data and Live Migration networks). VM Network traffic does not require "
"host IPs since VMs get their own addresses."
msgstr ""
"Configure el direccionamiento IP para los tipos de tráfico que requieren IPs a nivel de host "
"(redes de Data y Live Migration). El tráfico de Red de VM no requiere "
"IPs de host ya que las VMs obtienen sus propias direcciones."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:255
msgid "IPv4 Settings with Data (General) and Live Migration on different networks"
msgstr "Configuración IPv4 con Data (General) y Live Migration en redes diferentes"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:255
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_ipv4_settings.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_ipv4_settings.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:258
msgid "For each traffic type requiring IP configuration:"
msgstr "Para cada tipo de tráfico que requiere configuración de IP:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:260
msgid ""
"**Start IP Address** — The first IP in the range to assign to hosts. Each"
" host in the cluster receives the next sequential IP."
msgstr ""
"**Start IP Address** — La primera IP del rango a asignar a los hosts. Cada"
" host del clúster recibe la siguiente IP secuencial."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:261
msgid "**Subnet Mask** — Network subnet mask (e.g., ``255.255.255.0``)"
msgstr "**Subnet Mask** — Máscara de subred de la red (por ejemplo, ``255.255.255.0``)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:262
msgid "**Default Gateway** — Gateway for this traffic network"
msgstr "**Default Gateway** — Puerta de enlace para esta red de tráfico"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:263
msgid ""
"**Auto Apply to Servers** — When enabled, the IP addresses are "
"automatically distributed and applied to all current cluster hosts"
msgstr ""
"**Auto Apply to Servers** — Cuando está habilitado, las direcciones IP se "
"distribuyen y aplican automáticamente a todos los hosts actuales del clúster"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:265
msgid ""
"Gateways specified for Data (General), Live Migration, and iSCSI segments"
" are stored as **metadata only** within the Virtual Switch configuration."
" They are **not** applied to the host routing table. Only the "
"**Management Gateway** (configured during cluster provisioning) is "
"actively used for routing. These gateway values are retained for "
"documentation and future reference purposes."
msgstr ""
"Las puertas de enlace especificadas para los segmentos Data (General), Live Migration e iSCSI"
" se almacenan solo como **metadatos** dentro de la configuración del Switch Virtual."
" **No** se aplican a la tabla de enrutamiento del host. Solo la "
"**puerta de enlace de gestión** (configurada durante el aprovisionamiento del clúster) se "
"utiliza activamente para el enrutamiento. Estos valores de puerta de enlace se conservan con fines "
"de documentación y referencia futura."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:267
msgid ""
"When **Data (General) and Live Migration are on different networks**, "
"separate IP configuration sections appear for each traffic type, allowing"
" you to place them on different subnets."
msgstr ""
"Cuando **Data (General) y Live Migration están en redes diferentes**, "
"aparecen secciones de configuración de IP separadas para cada tipo de tráfico, lo que le permite"
" ubicarlos en subredes diferentes."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:269
msgid "IPv4 Settings for a single traffic type"
msgstr "Configuración IPv4 para un solo tipo de tráfico"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:269
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_ipv4_single_type.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_ipv4_single_type.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:272
msgid ""
"**Switch to Advanced Mode** — Enables per-host IP assignment for "
"scenarios where automatic sequential allocation is not appropriate."
msgstr ""
"**Switch to Advanced Mode** — Habilita la asignación de IP por host para "
"escenarios donde la asignación secuencial automática no es apropiada."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:275
msgid "Step 4: Port Settings"
msgstr "Paso 4: Configuración de puertos"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:277
msgid "Configure VLAN tagging and MTU settings."
msgstr "Configure el etiquetado de VLAN y los ajustes de MTU."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:279
msgid "Port Settings with VLAN ID and MTU"
msgstr "Configuración de puertos con ID de VLAN y MTU"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:279
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_port_settings.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_port_settings.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:282
msgid ""
"**VLAN ID per Traffic Type** — Optional VLAN tag (2–4094) applied to the "
"traffic. When set, traffic is tagged with this VLAN ID on the physical "
"uplink. Leave empty for untagged (native VLAN) traffic. VLAN 1 is "
"reserved and cannot be specified."
msgstr ""
"**VLAN ID per Traffic Type** — Etiqueta VLAN opcional (2–4094) aplicada al "
"tráfico. Cuando se establece, el tráfico se etiqueta con este ID de VLAN en el "
"uplink físico. Deje vacío para tráfico sin etiquetar (VLAN nativa). La VLAN 1 está "
"reservada y no se puede especificar."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:284
msgid ""
"When a VLAN ID is configured, the upstream physical switch ports must be "
"configured as trunk ports that allow the specified VLAN(s). Omitting the "
"VLAN ID means the traffic is sent untagged on the native VLAN of the "
"switch port."
msgstr ""
"Cuando se configura un ID de VLAN, los puertos del switch físico upstream deben "
"configurarse como puertos trunk que permitan las VLANs especificadas. Omitir el "
"ID de VLAN significa que el tráfico se envía sin etiquetar en la VLAN nativa del "
"puerto del switch."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:286
msgid ""
"**Global MTU** — Maximum Transmission Unit size for all interfaces in "
"this Virtual Switch. Options:"
msgstr ""
"**Global MTU** — Tamaño de la Unidad Máxima de Transmisión para todas las interfaces en "
"este Switch Virtual. Opciones:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:288
msgid "**1500** — Standard MTU (default)"
msgstr "**1500** — MTU estándar (predeterminado)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:289
msgid "**9000** — Jumbo frames, when required by the network design"
msgstr "**9000** — Tramas jumbo, cuando lo requiere el diseño de red"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:291
msgid ""
"Select MTU 9000 only when the complete path—including host interfaces, "
"switches, routers, and storage endpoints—has been configured and "
"validated for jumbo frames. Otherwise retain the default MTU 1500. The "
"MTU is optional in the product configuration; 9000 is not a universal HVM"
" requirement."
msgstr ""
"Seleccione MTU 9000 solo cuando la ruta completa—incluyendo interfaces de host, "
"switches, routers y endpoints de almacenamiento—haya sido configurada y "
"validada para tramas jumbo. De lo contrario, mantenga el MTU predeterminado 1500. El "
"MTU es opcional en la configuración del producto; 9000 no es un requisito universal de HVM."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:293
msgid "Port Settings for a single traffic type"
msgstr "Configuración de puertos para un solo tipo de tráfico"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:293
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_port_settings_single.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_port_settings_single.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:297
msgid "Step 5: Review"
msgstr "Paso 5: Revisión"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:299
msgid "Review the complete Virtual Switch configuration before applying."
msgstr "Revise la configuración completa del Switch Virtual antes de aplicar."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:301
msgid "Review step showing complete configuration summary"
msgstr "Paso de revisión mostrando el resumen completo de configuración"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:301
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_review.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_review.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:304
msgid "The review displays:"
msgstr "La revisión muestra:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:306
msgid "**Name** — Virtual Switch name"
msgstr "**Name** — Nombre del Switch Virtual"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:307
msgid "**Traffic Types** — Selected traffic types"
msgstr "**Traffic Types** — Tipos de tráfico seleccionados"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:308
msgid "**Bond Mode** — Bond configuration"
msgstr "**Bond Mode** — Configuración de bond"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:309
msgid "**Uplink NICs** — Per-host NIC assignments"
msgstr "**Uplink NICs** — Asignaciones de NIC por host"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:311
msgid ""
"Click **Finish** to create the Virtual Switch. The configuration is "
"applied to all hosts in the cluster."
msgstr ""
"Haga clic en **Finish** para crear el Switch Virtual. La configuración se "
"aplica a todos los hosts del clúster."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:314
msgid "Editing a Virtual Switch"
msgstr "Editar un Switch Virtual"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:316
msgid ""
"Click the edit icon (pencil) next to a Virtual Switch to modify its "
"configuration. You can change:"
msgstr ""
"Haga clic en el icono de edición (lápiz) junto a un Switch Virtual para modificar su "
"configuración. Puede cambiar:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:318
msgid "Uplink NICs (add/remove interfaces)"
msgstr "NICs de uplink (agregar/eliminar interfaces)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:319
msgid "Bond mode"
msgstr "Modo de bond"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:320
msgid "VLAN tags"
msgstr "Etiquetas VLAN"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:321
msgid "MTU settings"
msgstr "Ajustes de MTU"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:322
msgid "IP addresses"
msgstr "Direcciones IP"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:323
msgid "Traffic types"
msgstr "Tipos de tráfico"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:325
msgid ""
"Editing a Virtual Switch that is actively carrying traffic may cause a "
"brief network interruption as the new configuration is applied across "
"hosts. Specifically, changing uplinks, bond mode, MTU, or VLAN settings "
"will temporarily disrupt traffic on the affected networks. Plan these "
"changes during a maintenance window for production environments."
msgstr ""
"Editar un Switch Virtual que está transportando tráfico activamente puede causar una "
"breve interrupción de red mientras la nueva configuración se aplica en todos los "
"hosts. Específicamente, cambiar uplinks, modo de bond, MTU o configuración de VLAN "
"interrumpirá temporalmente el tráfico en las redes afectadas. Planifique estos "
"cambios durante una ventana de mantenimiento para entornos de producción."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:328
msgid "Deleting a Virtual Switch"
msgstr "Eliminar un Switch Virtual"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:330
msgid ""
"Click the delete icon (trash) next to a Virtual Switch to remove it. A "
"confirmation dialog appears before the deletion proceeds."
msgstr ""
"Haga clic en el icono de eliminación (papelera) junto a un Switch Virtual para eliminarlo. "
"Aparece un diálogo de confirmación antes de que proceda la eliminación."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:332
msgid "Delete Virtual Switch confirmation dialog"
msgstr "Diálogo de confirmación para eliminar Switch Virtual"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:332
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_delete_confirm.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: "
"/images/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches/vs_delete_confirm.png"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:337
msgid ""
"You cannot delete a Virtual Switch that has active VMs or networks "
"attached to it."
msgstr ""
"No puede eliminar un Switch Virtual que tenga VMs o redes activas "
"asociadas."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:338
msgid ""
"Deleting a Virtual Switch removes all associated host networking "
"configuration (bridges, bonds, VLANs) from every node in the cluster."
msgstr ""
"Eliminar un Switch Virtual elimina toda la configuración de red del host "
"asociada (bridges, bonds, VLANs) de cada nodo del clúster."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:339
msgid ""
"The default ``vs0`` should not be deleted unless you have an alternative "
"VM network configured."
msgstr ""
"El ``vs0`` predeterminado no debe eliminarse a menos que tenga una red de VM "
"alternativa configurada."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:342
msgid "Virtual Switch Best Practices"
msgstr "Mejores prácticas de Switches Virtuales"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:345
msgid "Network Design"
msgstr "Diseño de red"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:347
msgid ""
"**Separate traffic types for production environments.** Use dedicated "
"Virtual Switches for VM, storage, and migration traffic to avoid "
"contention and simplify troubleshooting."
msgstr ""
"**Separe los tipos de tráfico para entornos de producción.** Use Switches "
"Virtuales dedicados para el tráfico de VM, almacenamiento y migración para evitar "
"contención y simplificar la resolución de problemas."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:348
msgid "**Use at least 4 NICs per host** for proper traffic segregation:"
msgstr "**Use al menos 4 NICs por host** para una segregación adecuada del tráfico:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:350
msgid "2 NICs (bonded) for VM Network"
msgstr "2 NICs (en bond) para Red de VM"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:351
msgid "2 NICs (bonded) for Data/Live Migration"
msgstr "2 NICs (en bond) para Data/Live Migration"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:353
msgid ""
"**If only 2 NICs are available**, you can combine VM Network + Data "
"(General) + Live Migration on a single bonded Virtual Switch. Use VLANs "
"to segregate traffic logically."
msgstr ""
"**Si solo hay 2 NICs disponibles**, puede combinar Red de VM + Data "
"(General) + Live Migration en un solo Switch Virtual con bond. Use VLANs "
"para segregar el tráfico lógicamente."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:356
msgid "Bond Mode Selection"
msgstr "Selección del modo de bond"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:358
msgid ""
"**Active Backup** is recommended for most environments. It provides "
"simple redundancy with no switch-side configuration required."
msgstr ""
"**Active Backup** se recomienda para la mayoría de los entornos. Proporciona "
"redundancia simple sin necesidad de configuración en el switch."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:359
msgid ""
"**LACP (802.3ad)** uses both links and requires a matching LACP group on "
"the upstream physical switch. Validate the bond and failover before "
"carrying production traffic."
msgstr ""
"**LACP (802.3ad)** utiliza ambos enlaces y requiere un grupo LACP coincidente en "
"el switch físico upstream. Valide el bond y la conmutación por error antes de "
"transportar tráfico de producción."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:360
msgid ""
"**No Bonding** is appropriate for non-critical traffic or environments "
"with limited NIC availability. Not recommended for production VM "
"networks."
msgstr ""
"**Sin bonding** es apropiado para tráfico no crítico o entornos "
"con disponibilidad limitada de NICs. No se recomienda para redes de VM de producción."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:363
msgid "VLAN Configuration"
msgstr "Configuración de VLAN"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:365
msgid ""
"Use VLANs to segregate different traffic types when they share the same "
"physical uplinks."
msgstr ""
"Use VLANs para segregar diferentes tipos de tráfico cuando comparten los mismos "
"uplinks físicos."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:366
msgid ""
"Ensure the upstream switch ports are configured as trunk ports carrying "
"the required VLAN IDs."
msgstr ""
"Asegúrese de que los puertos del switch upstream estén configurados como puertos trunk que transporten "
"los IDs de VLAN requeridos."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:367
msgid ""
"Document your VLAN assignments to avoid conflicts and simplify "
"troubleshooting."
msgstr ""
"Documente sus asignaciones de VLAN para evitar conflictos y simplificar "
"la resolución de problemas."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:370
msgid "When to Use Tagged Bonds (VLAN-Tagged Bond Interfaces)"
msgstr "Cuándo usar bonds etiquetados (Interfaces de bond con etiqueta VLAN)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:372
msgid ""
"A **tagged bond** is a bonded interface (two or more NICs) that carries "
"multiple VLAN-tagged traffic types over the same physical link pair. This"
" is the most common production design pattern for HVM clusters."
msgstr ""
"Un **bond etiquetado** es una interfaz en bond (dos o más NICs) que transporta "
"múltiples tipos de tráfico con etiqueta VLAN sobre el mismo par de enlaces físicos. Este"
" es el patrón de diseño de producción más común para clústeres HVM."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:374
msgid "**Use tagged bonds when:**"
msgstr "**Use bonds etiquetados cuando:**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:376
msgid ""
"You have limited physical NICs (2–4 per host) but need to separate "
"multiple traffic types (VM, storage, migration)"
msgstr ""
"Tiene NICs físicas limitadas (2–4 por host) pero necesita separar "
"múltiples tipos de tráfico (VM, almacenamiento, migración)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:377
msgid ""
"You want link redundancy (bond) AND traffic isolation (VLANs) on the same"
" physical uplinks"
msgstr ""
"Desea redundancia de enlace (bond) Y aislamiento de tráfico (VLANs) en los mismos"
" uplinks físicos"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:378
msgid ""
"You are replicating a VMware design where a single vSwitch with multiple "
"port groups (each with a VLAN ID) carried different traffic types"
msgstr ""
"Está replicando un diseño de VMware donde un solo vSwitch con múltiples "
"grupos de puertos (cada uno con un ID de VLAN) transportaba diferentes tipos de tráfico"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:380
msgid "**How it works in Virtual Switch:**"
msgstr "**Cómo funciona en el Switch Virtual:**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:382
msgid ""
"A single Virtual Switch with a bonded uplink (Active-Backup or LACP) can "
"carry multiple traffic types, each on a separate VLAN. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Un solo Switch Virtual con un uplink en bond (Active-Backup o LACP) puede "
"transportar múltiples tipos de tráfico, cada uno en una VLAN separada. Por ejemplo:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:389
msgid "VLAN ID"
msgstr "ID de VLAN"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:392
msgid "100"
msgstr "100"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:393
msgid "Guest VM traffic, tagged on VLAN 100"
msgstr "Tráfico de VM invitada, etiquetado en VLAN 100"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:395
msgid "200"
msgstr "200"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:396
msgid "NFS storage traffic to storage array, tagged on VLAN 200"
msgstr "Tráfico de almacenamiento NFS hacia la matriz de almacenamiento, etiquetado en VLAN 200"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:398
msgid "300"
msgstr "300"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:399
msgid "VM memory transfer during live migration, tagged on VLAN 300"
msgstr "Transferencia de memoria de VM durante la migración en vivo, etiquetado en VLAN 300"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:401
msgid ""
"In this design, the upstream physical switch ports must be configured as "
"**trunk ports** allowing VLANs 100, 200, and 300. The bond provides link "
"redundancy; the VLAN tags provide traffic isolation."
msgstr ""
"En este diseño, los puertos del switch físico upstream deben configurarse como "
"**puertos trunk** que permitan las VLANs 100, 200 y 300. El bond proporciona redundancia "
"de enlace; las etiquetas VLAN proporcionan aislamiento de tráfico."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:403
msgid ""
"**VMware analogy:** This is equivalent to a VMware vSwitch with multiple "
"port groups, each assigned a different VLAN ID, all sharing the same "
"physical uplinks in a NIC team."
msgstr ""
"**Analogía con VMware:** Esto es equivalente a un vSwitch de VMware con múltiples "
"grupos de puertos, cada uno asignado a un ID de VLAN diferente, todos compartiendo los mismos "
"uplinks físicos en un equipo de NIC."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:405
msgid "**When NOT to use tagged bonds:**"
msgstr "**Cuándo NO usar bonds etiquetados:**"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:407
msgid ""
"If you have enough physical NICs to dedicate separate bonds to each "
"traffic type (e.g., 8+ NICs per host), separate Virtual Switches without "
"VLANs are simpler to troubleshoot"
msgstr ""
"Si tiene suficientes NICs físicas para dedicar bonds separados a cada "
"tipo de tráfico (por ejemplo, 8+ NICs por host), los Switches Virtuales separados sin "
"VLANs son más fáciles de diagnosticar"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:408
msgid "If your physical switch infrastructure does not support VLAN trunking"
msgstr "Si su infraestructura de switches físicos no soporta trunking de VLAN"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:409
msgid ""
"For iSCSI traffic that requires dedicated non-bonded NICs for multipath "
"(use a separate iSCSI Virtual Switch instead)"
msgstr ""
"Para tráfico iSCSI que requiere NICs dedicadas sin bond para multipath "
"(use un Switch Virtual iSCSI separado en su lugar)"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:412
msgid "MTU Recommendations"
msgstr "Recomendaciones de MTU"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:414
msgid "**VM Network**: Standard MTU (1500) is usually sufficient."
msgstr "**Red de VM**: El MTU estándar (1500) suele ser suficiente."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:415
msgid ""
"**Data (General)**: Use the MTU required by the end-to-end storage "
"network design."
msgstr ""
"**Data (General)**: Use el MTU requerido por el diseño de red de almacenamiento "
"de extremo a extremo."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:416
msgid ""
"**Data (iSCSI)**: Use the MTU required by the end-to-end storage network "
"design."
msgstr ""
"**Data (iSCSI)**: Use el MTU requerido por el diseño de red de almacenamiento "
"de extremo a extremo."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:417
msgid ""
"**Live Migration**: Use a consistent MTU across the complete migration "
"path."
msgstr ""
"**Live Migration**: Use un MTU consistente en toda la ruta de migración."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:418
msgid "**SDN**: Match your SDN controller requirements."
msgstr "**SDN**: Coincida con los requisitos de su controlador SDN."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:420
msgid ""
"All devices in the network path (host NICs, switches, routers, storage "
"arrays) must support the configured MTU. A mismatch will cause packet "
"fragmentation or drops."
msgstr ""
"Todos los dispositivos en la ruta de red (NICs del host, switches, routers, matrices "
"de almacenamiento) deben soportar el MTU configurado. Una discrepancia causará "
"fragmentación o pérdida de paquetes."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:423
msgid "Virtual Switch Limitations"
msgstr "Limitaciones de los Switches Virtuales"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:425
msgid "Maximum **8 Virtual Switches** per cluster."
msgstr "Máximo **8 Switches Virtuales** por clúster."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:426
msgid "Virtual Switch names are limited to **12 characters**."
msgstr "Los nombres de los Switches Virtuales están limitados a **12 caracteres**."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:427
msgid "Each Virtual Switch supports **1 or 2 uplink NICs** per host."
msgstr "Cada Switch Virtual soporta **1 o 2 NICs de uplink** por host."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:428
msgid ""
"**iSCSI** Virtual Switches are limited to a single NIC (no bonding) — "
"multipath is handled at the protocol layer."
msgstr ""
"Los Switches Virtuales **iSCSI** están limitados a una sola NIC (sin bonding) — "
"el multipath se gestiona en la capa de protocolo."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:429
msgid "**SDN** Virtual Switches cannot share uplinks with other traffic types."
msgstr "Los Switches Virtuales **SDN** no pueden compartir uplinks con otros tipos de tráfico."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:430
msgid ""
"Bond mode changes on an active Virtual Switch may cause brief "
"connectivity interruption."
msgstr ""
"Los cambios de modo de bond en un Switch Virtual activo pueden causar una breve "
"interrupción de conectividad."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:431
msgid ""
"All hosts in the cluster must have the selected uplink NIC(s) available. "
"When using **Uniform uplinks**, ensure consistent NIC naming across "
"hosts. When using **Set uplink NICs per host**, each host must have its "
"individually assigned NIC(s) available."
msgstr ""
"Todos los hosts del clúster deben tener las NICs de uplink seleccionadas disponibles. "
"Al usar **Uniform uplinks**, asegúrese de que los nombres de NIC sean consistentes entre "
"los hosts. Al usar **Set uplink NICs per host**, cada host debe tener sus "
"NICs asignadas individualmente disponibles."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:432
msgid ""
"Only **one Live Migration interface** is allowed per cluster. You cannot "
"configure Live Migration on multiple Virtual Switches."
msgstr ""
"Solo se permite **una interfaz de Live Migration** por clúster. No puede "
"configurar Live Migration en múltiples Switches Virtuales."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:433
msgid ""
"When adding **Data (General)** or **Live Migration** segments to the "
"management Virtual Switch (``vs0``), VLAN tagging is required for each "
"segment."
msgstr ""
"Al agregar segmentos de **Data (General)** o **Live Migration** al "
"Switch Virtual de gestión (``vs0``), se requiere el etiquetado de VLAN para cada "
"segmento."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:436
msgid "Virtual Switch Troubleshooting"
msgstr "Resolución de problemas de Switches Virtuales"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:441
msgid "Read-only Host Verification"
msgstr "Verificación de host de solo lectura"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:443
msgid ""
"Use the UI to change Virtual Switch configuration. On a layout 2.0 host, "
"the following ``hvmcli`` commands are read-only and can be used to "
"compare host state with the cluster's **Network** tab:"
msgstr ""
"Use la interfaz de usuario para cambiar la configuración del Switch Virtual. En un host de diseño 2.0, "
"los siguientes comandos de ``hvmcli`` son de solo lectura y pueden usarse para "
"comparar el estado del host con la pestaña **Network** del clúster:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:445
msgid ""
"sudo hvmcli virtswitch list\n"
"sudo hvmcli virtswitch show --virtswitch-name <virtual-switch-name>\n"
"sudo hvmcli virtswitch status --virtswitch-name <virtual-switch-name> "
"--json\n"
"sudo hvmcli network list"
msgstr ""
"sudo hvmcli virtswitch list\n"
"sudo hvmcli virtswitch show --virtswitch-name <virtual-switch-name>\n"
"sudo hvmcli virtswitch status --virtswitch-name <virtual-switch-name> "
"--json\n"
"sudo hvmcli network list"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:452
msgid ""
"Names, interfaces, addresses, and status values vary by cluster. The "
"detailed view reports the managed uplink, bond mode, MTU, traffic "
"segments, and optional VLAN IDs. An untagged segment has no VLAN ID. Do "
"not use ``create``, ``edit``, ``add-segment``, ``delete-segment``, or "
"``delete`` as diagnostic commands; they mutate host networking."
msgstr ""
"Los nombres, interfaces, direcciones y valores de estado varían según el clúster. La "
"vista detallada informa el uplink gestionado, modo de bond, MTU, segmentos de tráfico "
"e IDs de VLAN opcionales. Un segmento sin etiquetar no tiene ID de VLAN. No "
"use ``create``, ``edit``, ``add-segment``, ``delete-segment`` o "
"``delete`` como comandos de diagnóstico; estos modifican la configuración de red del host."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:454
msgid ""
"For an Active Backup bond, also inspect the effective host-side bond "
"configuration for MII polling, up-delay, and down-delay. The read-only "
"Virtual Switch output does not establish that any particular values were "
"applied. If the supported UI or ``hvmcli`` version does not expose these "
"settings, use the release-specific supported inspection and configuration"
" procedure supplied by HPE Support before placing the bond in service."
msgstr ""
"Para un bond Active Backup, también inspeccione la configuración efectiva del bond "
"en el lado del host para sondeo MII, up-delay y down-delay. La salida de solo lectura "
"del Switch Virtual no establece que se hayan aplicado valores particulares. "
"Si la versión soportada de la interfaz de usuario o ``hvmcli`` no expone estos "
"ajustes, use el procedimiento de inspección y configuración específico de la versión "
"proporcionado por el soporte de HPE antes de poner el bond en servicio."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:457
msgid "Virtual Switch Not Applying"
msgstr "El Switch Virtual no se aplica"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:459
msgid "If a Virtual Switch fails to apply to a host:"
msgstr "Si un Switch Virtual no se aplica a un host:"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:461
msgid ""
"Check host connectivity from the cluster — ensure the host is reachable "
"and the Morpheus agent is running."
msgstr ""
"Verifique la conectividad del host desde el clúster — asegúrese de que el host sea accesible "
"y que el agente de Morpheus esté en ejecución."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:462
msgid ""
"Review ``/var/log/hvmcli/`` on the affected host for detailed error "
"messages."
msgstr ""
"Revise ``/var/log/hvmcli/`` en el host afectado para mensajes de error detallados."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:463
msgid "Verify the selected uplink NICs exist and are up on the host."
msgstr "Verifique que las NICs de uplink seleccionadas existan y estén activas en el host."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:464
msgid ""
"Check that no conflicting network configuration exists in "
"``/etc/netplan/``."
msgstr ""
"Verifique que no exista una configuración de red en conflicto en "
"``/etc/netplan/``."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:467
msgid "LACP Bond Not Working"
msgstr "El bond LACP no funciona"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:469
msgid "Verify that LACP is configured on the upstream physical switch ports."
msgstr "Verifique que LACP esté configurado en los puertos del switch físico upstream."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:470
msgid "Ensure both switch and host are using the same LACP mode (802.3ad)."
msgstr "Asegúrese de que tanto el switch como el host estén usando el mismo modo LACP (802.3ad)."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:471
msgid ""
"Check that both uplink NICs have physical link (green LED or ``ip link "
"show`` state UP)."
msgstr ""
"Verifique que ambas NICs de uplink tengan enlace físico (LED verde o estado UP en ``ip link "
"show``)."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:474
msgid "VM Network Connectivity Issues"
msgstr "Problemas de conectividad de red de VM"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:476
msgid ""
"Verify the Virtual Switch bridge is up: check ``ip link show`` on the "
"host for the bridge device (``<name>-br``)."
msgstr ""
"Verifique que el bridge del Switch Virtual esté activo: compruebe ``ip link show`` en el "
"host para el dispositivo bridge (``<name>-br``)."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:477
msgid ""
"If using VLANs, confirm the upstream switch trunk port carries the "
"configured VLAN."
msgstr ""
"Si usa VLANs, confirme que el puerto trunk del switch upstream transporta la "
"VLAN configurada."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:478
msgid ""
"Check that libvirt network is active: ``virsh net-list`` should show the "
"Virtual Switch network as active."
msgstr ""
"Verifique que la red de libvirt esté activa: ``virsh net-list`` debería mostrar la "
"red del Switch Virtual como activa."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:481
msgid "Storage Network Unreachable"
msgstr "Red de almacenamiento inaccesible"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:483
msgid "Verify the IP was correctly assigned to the host interface."
msgstr "Verifique que la IP fue asignada correctamente a la interfaz del host."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:484
msgid ""
"Check that the storage array or NFS server is on the same subnet or "
"reachable via the configured gateway."
msgstr ""
"Verifique que la matriz de almacenamiento o el servidor NFS esté en la misma subred o "
"sea accesible a través de la puerta de enlace configurada."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:485
msgid "For iSCSI, verify multipath is configured correctly at the OS level."
msgstr "Para iSCSI, verifique que el multipath esté configurado correctamente a nivel del SO."
